# anthropic_federation_rule_workspace (Resource)

Enables a Workload Identity Federation (WIF) rule for an additional workspace. A federation rule's create-time `workspace_id` already enables it for one workspace — this resource manages the extra workspaces a rule should also be usable from. Do not also manage that first workspace with this resource, or Terraform and the API will fight over the same enablement.

> **API**: `POST/GET/DELETE /v1/organizations/federation_rules/{federation_rule_id}/workspaces[/{workspace_id}]`.
> **Auth**: org:admin OAuth bearer token (`auth_token` / `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`). Admin API keys are not accepted.
> **Scope restriction**: OAuth callers (this provider) may only manage this enablement for rules whose `oauth_scope` is `workspace:developer` or `workspace:inference`; other scopes require a Console session.
> **Immutable**: every attribute forces replacement — there is no update endpoint.

